"time": "8000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn4le16ob04re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It's cold and there is a problem with the power in this hotel, too. I had to shower in the dark. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Concierge</span>: I'm so sorry. How's your trip going apart from that? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Good, so far. I went to the Great Wall two days ago. <br/>", "time": "12000", "id": 3}, {"image": "engenn4le16ob04re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Concierge</span>: It's the best attraction in China.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I don't know about that. There are a lot of steps and I'm still a little sore. Oh \u2026 and the crowds. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Concierge</span>: Ok, your taxi is here.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Thank you. <br/>", "time": "32000", "id": 4}, {"image": "engenn4le16ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Concierge</span>: Watch your step, Miss. Don't trip on the wet floor.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yes, I don't want to fall on these tiles. <br/>", "time": "48400", "id": 5}, {"image": "engenn4le16ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Concierge</span>: These showers haven't stopped. Take this umbrella on the house. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  Great, thanks.", "time": "57000", "id": 6}]}}], "id": 1}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally in China", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Fall and Fall", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information in a limited range of social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "concierge ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an employee at a hotel who gives help and information to the people staying at the hotel", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The concierge gave the tour group directions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you travel.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "authentic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "real or genuine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We went to an authentic noodle shop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tile", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a flat piece of hard clay or stone you use to cover walls or floors", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't slip on the tile floor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fall ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to come or go down quickly from a high place or position", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally fell on the stairs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "floor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the part of a room on which you stand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally spilled her coffee on the floor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sore", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling or affected by pain", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My feet are sore from walking all day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dark", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place where little or no light can be seen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally had a shower in the dark.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on the house", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when a business (hotel, restaurant) gives something for free", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Here is an umbrella on the house.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Homonyms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Homonyms, are words that have the same spelling and the same pronunciation but have different meanings.  <br/><br/>For example: <span class=\"italic\">trip</span>, <span class=\"italic\">fall</span> and <span class=\"italic\">shower</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Sally is on a trip to China. (noun: a journey to a place) <br/>Sally tripped on the stairs. (verb: to fall or almost fall)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is a nice fall day. (noun: the season when leaves fall from trees)   <br/>I don't want to fall on the wet floor. (verb: to go down to a lower position)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had a shower at 8 o'clock. (noun: bathing under falling water) <br/>There were a lot of showers today. (noun: a fall of rain)", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Uncertainty", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "If you are not sure whether something can or can not happen, you can use: ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Rising intonation</span> makes you sound uncertain about what you're saying. Uncertainty can also have <span class=\"strong\">falling intonation</span>.  It depends on the speaker.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rising Intonation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Falling Intonation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Using: \u201c<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Well, \u2026</span>\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Using: \u201c<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I suppose \u2026 but \u2026</span>\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm not sure.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's impossible.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I doubt it.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It might be.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have my doubts.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It might not be.\\\"}\",\"\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Find 5 new homonyms online or in a dictionary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5 sentences using the same word two times. Example:<span class=\"italic\"> My great-grandfather was a great man.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I find homonyms on the Internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write 5 sentences using homonyms.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice saying homonyms aloud.", "type": "text"}]}]}